(vector (map (:adr/governor-name-collision-survey-9312 "before selecting this vertical, every remaining :blueprint-tier candidate's own :itonami.blueprint/governor keyword was compared directly against every already-implemented sibling's own governor name -- 9 of the other 11 candidates (7220, 8522, 8549, 9411, 9512, 9522, 9523, 9524, 9529) were found to declare the IDENTICAL governor keyword as an already-implemented sibling (research-integrity-governor colliding with research/7210; curriculum-safeguarding-governor colliding with secondary/8521; instruction-integrity-governor colliding with cultural/8542; association-governance-governor colliding with association/9412; repair-shop-governor colliding with repairshop/9521, five times over). ISIC 9312's own :membership-governor was confirmed distinct from association/9412's, congregation/9491's and union/9420's own governor names -- the strongest remaining candidate"), (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607081900-cloud-itonami-advertising-7310-coverage" "2607082100-cloud-itonami-polling-7320-coverage" "2607082200-cloud-itonami-research-7210-coverage" "2607082300-cloud-itonami-design-7410-coverage" "2607082600-cloud-itonami-nursing-8710-coverage" "2607082800-cloud-itonami-sports-8541-coverage" "2607082900-cloud-itonami-alliedhealth-8690-coverage" "2607083000-cloud-itonami-laundry-9601-coverage" "2607083300-cloud-itonami-holdco-6420-coverage" "2607083500-cloud-itonami-photo-7420-coverage" "2607083600-cloud-itonami-personalservice-9609-coverage" "2607083800-cloud-itonami-edsupport-8550-coverage" "2607084000-cloud-itonami-headoffice-7010-coverage" "2607084300-cloud-itonami-residential-8790-coverage" "2607084400-cloud-itonami-cultural-8542-coverage" "2607084600-cloud-itonami-reserve-6411-coverage" "2607084700-kotoba-lang-apn-cloud-itonami-isic-6110" "2607085600-cloud-itonami-proserv-7490-coverage" "2607085700-cloud-itonami-sportsevent-9319-coverage" "2607085800-cloud-itonami-recreation-9329-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic- ADR-0001s" "langgraph ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/lesson-applied-proactively-9312 "tested via :conduct/screen directly from the start (not via the actuation op against an unscreened member), applying parksafety's ADR-2607071922 Decision 5 / eldercare's, museum's, conservation's, salon's, entertainment's, casework's, hospital's, facility's, school's, association's, leasing's, behavioral's, secondary's, card's, water's, telecom's, aerospace's, recovery's, consulting's, union's, congregation's, fab's, energy's, care's, navigator's, learning's, banking's, advertising's, polling's, research's, design's, nursing's, sports's, alliedhealth's, laundry's, holdco's, photo's, personalservice's, edsupport's, headoffice's, residential's, cultural's, reserve's, proserv's, sportsevent's and recreation's ADR-0001 lesson PROACTIVELY for a forty-sixth consecutive vertical"), (:adr/id "2607085900"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 73, :blueprint 12, :spec 545, :total 630}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/honest-reuse-check-1-9312 "disciplinary-complaint-unresolved-violations is an HONEST reuse of association.governor/complaint-unresolved-violations's own concept (ISIC 9412), the 58th distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix; most recently recreation.governor/emergency-egress-obstructed-violations at 57th) -- NOT claimed as new"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/honest-reuse-check-2-9312 "appeal-window-still-open? is an HONEST reuse of personalservice.registry/cooling-off-period-not-elapsed?'s own MINIMUM-threshold sufficiency SHAPE (the eighth instance of that family), the TENTH instance overall, applied to a genuinely different real-world concept: a nonprofit membership-organization due-process appeal/notice period before a member suspension or expulsion may be finalized (Germany's BGB §35 Vereinsrecht, California Corporations Code §7341, Japan's 一般社団法人及び一般財団法人に関する法律 第25条), not a consumer cooling-off right -- NOT claimed as a new shape"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607085900: `cloud-itonami-isic-9312` (activities of sports clubs) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607080100 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9412`, association -- `complaint-unresolved-violations` origin)\n- ADR-2607083600 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9609`, personalservice -- `cooling-off-period-not-elapsed?` origin)\n- ADR-2607085800 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9329`, other amusement/recreation)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-9312/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-9312` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\nactivities of sports clubs: membership-based athletic and sporting\nclubs. Like every prior vertical in this fleet, the blueprint text\nalone is not an implementation -- this ADR records the governed-actor\nbuild that promotes `cloud-itonami-isic-9312` from `:blueprint` to\n`:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry, the fifty-\nninth vertical built outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/\nreal-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-9312`'s blueprint described a real-world\n   sports-club operating model (member enrollment intake, membership-\n   governance verification, membership-suspension/expulsion\n   finalization) but had no governed-actor implementation: no Store,\n   no Governor, no rollout phasing, no tests.\n2. The blueprint's own text names only ONE real-world act\n   (\"finalizing a membership suspension or expulsion\") -- this build\n   needed the single-actuation shape.\n3. Before selecting this vertical, a survey of all 12 remaining\n   `:blueprint`-tier candidates found that MOST were structurally\n   blocked: 9 of the other 11 declare a `:itonami.blueprint/governor`\n   keyword that is an EXACT collision with an already-implemented\n   sibling's own governor name (confirmed via direct `blueprint.edn`\n   comparison, not just a \"similar domain\" judgment). This needed to\n   be verified rigorously and documented, since it materially narrows\n   the fleet's remaining genuinely-buildable candidate pool.\n4. Given the check-family space for a membership-suspension/expulsion\n   actuation shape is already well covered by `association`/9412's\n   and `personalservice`/9609's own established concepts, this\n   build's own checks needed to be honestly characterized as reuses\n   rather than straining for an unearned novelty claim.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Single-actuation shape.** The blueprint's own README/business-\n   model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names only ONE\n   real-world act, with \"suspension\" and \"expulsion\" treated as ONE\n   conceptual act. Matching every prior single-actuation sibling's\n   shape, `high-stakes` is the one-member set `#{:actuation/finalize-\n   membership-action}` -- a POSITIVE actuation, matching this fleet's\n   majority shape (`3600`/`6190` are the two NEGATIVE-actuation\n   exceptions).\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `member`. Four ops:\n   `:member/intake`, `:eligibility/verify`, `:conduct/screen`,\n   `:actuation/finalize-membership-action` (high-stakes).\n3. **`disciplinary-complaint-unresolved-violations` -- an honest\n   reuse of `association`/9412's own concept, not claimed as new.**\n   The 58th distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation\n   discipline overall (`casualty.governor/sanctions-violations`'s\n   original fix; most recently `recreation.governor/emergency-\n   egress-obstructed-violations` at 57th). Gates `:conduct/screen` and\n   the actuation.\n4. **`appeal-window-still-open?` -- an honest reuse of\n   `personalservice`/9609's MINIMUM-threshold sufficiency SHAPE, for\n   a genuinely different real-world concept.** The tenth instance of\n   that family overall, comparing a member's own `:days-since-\n   suspension-notice` against its own `:minimum-appeal-window-days`\n   -- grounded in nonprofit membership-organization due-process law\n   (Germany's BGB §35, California Corporations Code §7341, Japan's\n   一般社団法人及び一般財団法人に関する法律 第25条), not a consumer\n   cooling-off right. Gates only the actuation.\n5. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean.** `:membership-action-\n   finalized?` on the `member` record, never a single `:status`\n   value.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/sportsclub/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor\n   is safely named `member` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** -- Phase 3's `:auto` set is\n   `{:member/intake}` only; the actuation is permanently excluded from\n   every phase's `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** -- this blueprint's own\n   `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies` names no domain-\n   specific capability beyond the generic stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** -- `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed** -- the `isic-`\n    prefixed `:id` and `:required-technologies`/`:optional-\n    technologies` already matched the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n    exactly; only the `:maturity` field itself needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Seventy-fourth implemented actor in this fleet's registry (73\n  implemented immediately before this build).\n- Documents an honest reuse of `association`/9412's own concept\n  (58th unconditional-eval grounding), not claimed as new.\n- Documents an honest reuse of `personalservice`/9609's MINIMUM-\n  threshold sufficiency SHAPE (10th instance), for a genuinely\n  different domain concept, not claimed as a new shape.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity is proven by `test/sportsclub/\n  store_contract_test.clj`.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 73 → 74, `:blueprint` 12 → 11,\n  `:spec` 545 unchanged (sum 630; see Scope note below on the\n  `:total` figure).\n- Test status: 30 tests / 132 assertions, lint clean, demo verified\n  end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four\n  HARD-hold cases).\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s full test suite re-run with the local-root\n  `technology` override before committing -- 7 tests / 121 assertions,\n  all green.\n- **Fleet-wide finding**: of the 11 other `:blueprint`-tier candidates\n  remaining at build time, 9 (`7220`, `8522`, `8549`, `9411`, `9512`,\n  `9522`, `9523`, `9524`, `9529`) are structurally blocked by an\n  exact governor-name collision with an already-implemented sibling\n  -- confirmed via direct `blueprint.edn` comparison, not inference.\n  This narrows the pool of genuinely distinct next candidates\n  considerably and should be re-checked (not assumed stale) at the\n  next vertical-selection point, since the registry is edited\n  concurrently by other sessions.\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Scope note\n\nThis ADR's `:fleet-maturity-before`/`:fleet-maturity-after` `:total`\nfield (630) reflects the actual observed sum of `:implemented` +\n`:blueprint` + `:spec` in `registry.edn` at build time, rather than\n`docs/cloud-itonami.md`'s \"Total entries: 643\" figure -- the same\nclarification ADR-2607085700's and ADR-2607085800's own scope notes\nalready recorded: that 643 figure tracks a separate, pre-existing,\nwider ISIC-class/group count, not per-vertical maturity accounting.\nNot introduced or worsened by this build; not in scope to reconcile\nhere.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| Building `cloud-itonami-isic-9411` (business/employers membership organizations) | Its own `:association-governance-governor` is an EXACT collision with `association`/9412's already-implemented governor name; also a live test fixture requiring a repoint if selected |\n| Building one of the repair-category candidates (9512/9522/9523/9524/9529) | All five declare the IDENTICAL `:repair-shop-governor` keyword already used by `repairshop`/9521 |\n| Forcing a \"genuinely new\" check to avoid an all-reuse build | The check-family space for this actuation shape is already well covered by `association`/9412's and `personalservice`/9609's own concepts; honest reuse characterization is more defensible than an unearned novelty claim |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9312/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9312/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9312/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9412/src/association/governor.cljc` (`complaint-unresolved-violations` origin)\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-9609/src/personalservice/registry.cljc` (`cooling-off-period-not-elapsed?` origin)\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"9312\"`)"), (:adr/test-status-9312 "30 tests / 132 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 121 assertions, all green"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 74, :blueprint 11, :spec 545, :total 630}"), (:adr/single-actuation-9312 "this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names only ONE real-world act (finalizing a membership suspension or expulsion, both terms treated as ONE conceptual act), so this build uses the single-actuation shape (#{:actuation/finalize-membership-action}); a POSITIVE actuation matching this fleet's majority shape (3600/6190 are the two NEGATIVE-actuation exceptions)"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR primarily to record a fleet-wide governor-name-collision observation (9 of 11 remaining :blueprint-tier candidates blocked) discovered while selecting this vertical, alongside the actor's own coverage promotion; per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention, an all-honest-reuse check family still warrants its own record when it is the vehicle for a genuinely new, load-bearing fleet-wide finding; :fleet-maturity-before/:total reflects the actual observed sum of the three maturity tiers in registry.edn at build time, not the docs/cloud-itonami.md 'Total entries: 643' figure (see ADR-2607085700's/2607085800's own scope notes for the same clarification)"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/blueprint-already-correct-9312 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"9312\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding"), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-9312"), (:adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-9312 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-9312 (activities of sports clubs) deepened to :implemented -- fifty-ninth vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/pattern-9312 "sealed ClubOps-LLM + independent Membership Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all seventy-two prior actors; FIFTY-NINTH build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419, 7310, 7320, 7210, 7410, 8710, 8541, 8690, 9601, 6420, 7420, 9609, 8550, 7010, 8790, 8542, 6411, 7490, 9319, 9329)")))